# LOCAL, sensitive block patterns — copy this file to `deny-patterns.local.txt`
# (which is gitignored) and fill in the concrete internal strings for THIS machine.
#
# Keep the real file OUT of the repo: it must never be committed, so the deny-list
# itself doesn't reveal the internals it protects.
#
# Extended regex, case-insensitive. One pattern per line. Examples:

# internal project / product code names
# \bProjectFalcon\b
# \bBlueHarbor\b

# customer names
# \bAcme (Industries|GmbH)\b

# internal hostnames / systems
# \b[a-z0-9-]+\.intra\.example-corp\.local\b
